            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for a guard, then the Persian for a street sweeper."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: پیاده شدن",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پیاده شدن — piyâde shodan — \"to get off (a vehicle)\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "piyâde shodan is \"to become on foot\": piyâde is inherited, from Middle Persian payādag, \"foot soldier\" (EtymDB, which also lists the sense \"chess pawn\"). shodan, \"to become\", is an inherited verb; it is usually traced to Middle Persian šudan, \"to go\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
